WEBVTT

00:00.497 --> 00:06.036 align:center line:79%
As we have this moment of adjustment
in our Sunday pattern at church,

00:06.837 --> 00:09.172 align:center line:79%
what are some of the things
that you think will help?

00:09.873 --> 00:12.109 align:center line:81%
Well, I'm gonna go to 80,000 feet.

00:12.109 --> 00:13.110 align:center line:81%
Yeah.

00:13.110 --> 00:14.244 align:center line:81%
Very overarching.

00:15.445 --> 00:22.185 align:center line:79%
Uh, every member of this church
has an individual responsibility to study

00:22.219 --> 00:27.891 align:center line:79%
and learn the doctrine of Christ, and then
strive to apply it in their lives.

00:30.427 --> 00:35.699 align:center line:79%
We cannot expect the Church
as an institution to provide

00:35.732 --> 00:38.068 align:center line:81%
to us everything that we need to know.

00:38.835 --> 00:43.040 align:center line:79%
There's a price that each of us has to pay
in terms of individual study.

00:43.840 --> 00:48.011 align:center line:79%
So we go to worship the Father
in the name of the Son,

00:48.912 --> 00:54.851 align:center line:79%
we go to participate in the ordinance
of the sacrament, and we go to learn.

00:56.787 --> 01:00.000 align:center line:79%
I think we can characterize the change
in the meeting schedule

01:00.000 --> 01:00.123 align:center line:79%
I think we can characterize the change
in the meeting schedule

01:00.324 --> 01:02.225 align:center line:81%
in a series of very simple questions.

01:03.360 --> 01:07.431 align:center line:79%
When I was a boy, young man,
you would go to church on Sunday,

01:08.298 --> 01:11.435 align:center line:79%
you would come home,
and the discussion question would be,

01:11.435 --> 01:13.503 align:center line:81%
"What did you learn at church today?"

01:14.671 --> 01:17.741 align:center line:81%
I think that world is gone, to a degree.

01:17.741 --> 01:18.742 align:center line:81%
Mm-hmm.

01:18.742 --> 01:21.244 align:center line:81%
I think now we return home from church,

01:22.746 --> 01:26.683 align:center line:79%
and what did you share at church
today that you learned during the week?

01:26.984 --> 01:28.118 align:center line:81%
Hmm.

01:28.585 --> 01:30.000 align:center line:79%
So we study daily, we study personally,
we do that all during the week,

01:30.000 --> 01:32.889 align:center line:79%
So we study daily, we study personally,
we do that all during the week,

01:33.624 --> 01:36.426 align:center line:79%
and then on Sunday,
we have the opportunity

01:36.593 --> 01:39.696 align:center line:79%
to counsel together
about what we are learning.

01:39.863 --> 01:45.002 align:center line:79%
So I think it all speaks
to home-centered, church-supported,

01:45.969 --> 01:49.106 align:center line:79%
and ongoing opportunities
to learn for ourself.

01:49.773 --> 01:52.809 align:center line:79%
When you think of preparing
for the sacrament meeting,

01:53.610 --> 01:57.648 align:center line:79%
anything stand out, anything particularly
important in, in our preparation?

01:58.582 --> 01:59.583 align:center line:81%
Yes.

02:00.484 --> 02:04.254 align:center line:79%
We can always retain
a remission of our sins.

02:04.521 --> 02:05.555 align:center line:81%
Mm-hmm.

02:06.423 --> 02:08.492 align:center line:81%
I think many members of the Church,

02:09.326 --> 02:13.597 align:center line:79%
uh, believe that when
we're baptized, we are cleansed,

02:14.765 --> 02:18.135 align:center line:79%
